# `=` in a `where` predicate: DS0110, with a fix to `==`. The tree reads it as a comparison.
mode: syntax
---- query
from 'orders.csv' | where customerId = "c-001"
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..47
  PIPELINE@0..46
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    LITERAL@5..17
      STRING@5..17 "'orders.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@17..18 " "
    PIPE@18..19 "|"
    WHITESPACE@19..20 " "
    WHERE_OP@20..46
      IDENT@20..25 "where"
      WHITESPACE@25..26 " "
      BIN_EXPR@26..46
        NAME_REF@26..36
          IDENT@26..36 "customerId"
        WHITESPACE@36..37 " "
        EQ@37..38 "="
        WHITESPACE@38..39 " "
        LITERAL@39..46
          STRING@39..46 "\"c-001\""
  WHITESPACE@46..47 "\n"

error[DS0110]: `=` is assignment, not comparison
  --> query:1:38
  |
1 | from 'orders.csv' | where customerId = "c-001"
  |                                      ^ assignment is not allowed here
  |
  = help: use `==` to compare values: `customerId == "c-001"`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    from 'orders.csv' | where customerId == "c-001"
which parses without errors
